    "body": "## Overview\n\nRequests for more logprobs than the vocabulary pass validation when `--max-logprobs` is larger than the vocab, then crash in `torch.topk`. Validation now caps the allowed count at the vocabulary size. Fixes #64291.\n\n## Claims\n\n- `SamplingParams(logprobs=20)._validate_logprobs` raises when `max_logprobs` is 20 and the vocab size is 10.\n- The same cap applies to `prompt_logprobs`.\n- A request for exactly the vocab size is still accepted.\n\n## Validation\n\n`python3 -m pytest tests/test_sampling_params.py::test_logprobs_above_vocab_size_are_rejected tests/test_sampling_params.py::test_non_diffusion_models_unaffected -q --noconftest`\n\nBefore the cap, the new test did not raise. After it, both tests passed. No GPU run: the worker `topk` crash is the consequence of the validation hole, and the test drives `_validate_logprobs`.\n\n## Details\n\n`_validate_logprobs` compared the request only with `model_config.max_logprobs`. That default is 20 and is not tied to the vocab. `topk` requires `k <= vocab`. The allowed maximum is now `min(max_logprobs, vocab_size)` when the vocab size is positive. `max_logprobs == -1` still means the full vocabulary.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
